  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Mounted observation and coordinates",
      "assessment": "Receives the actual host.view from one key-visible UIWindow; requires drawHierarchy completeness. The1x1 scale1 renderer is translated by negative bounds midpoint while drawing the original full-size bounds: a center crop, not a downsample of the complete view. It does not obtain observed bytes from the renderer fixture. The fixed360x240 preview/24x16 image share3:2 aspect and production centers the image with overlays at the bottom. The center is expected to lie inside the uniform image; safe-area/layout and capture reliability remain inferred until Apple execution. The first32 positive control fails rather than treating missing output as success."
    },
    {
      "topic": "sRGB, alpha and tolerance",
      "assessment": "The snapshot is redrawn into explicit8-bit sRGB premultiplied-last/big-endian RGBA.32\u00b12 and160\u00b12 are disjoint and exclude black/white empty backgrounds; uniform neutral interior reduces interpolation and gamut ambiguity. preferredRange.standard alone does not choose the exact pixel format. Because format.opaque=true, alpha255 is an output-format check, not source-image alpha/validity evidence. No measured color-conversion guarantee is claimed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Adoption ordering",
      "assessment": "Visible32 is required beforeB. B establishes its mock downgrade then suspends; A2 suspends on a separate continuation.32 is sampled before releasingA2, and160 only after release. Renderer, continuations,2A/1B counts, one mounted identity and cleanup are unchanged. A successful native run would support consultation and replacement-pixel adoption."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Coverage boundary",
      "assessment": "Held32 is one checkpoint whileA2 is suspended, not continuous visibility. No handshake waits for resumedB cancellation handling before that checkpoint. The cancellation is injected manually and outputs are synthetic. The pixel test does not assert backend badges, warnings, previous/current AX labels, VoiceOver, real GPU downgrade, pause or reattachment. A current-ticket label regression could survive this observer while pixels remain correct."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Counterfactual",
      "assessment": "The old cached-A shortcut should fail the preserved secondARequested/two-A checks, but original hook-only production before/fail remains unrun. The source342 AX-positive-control failure is the failed observer version, not that counterfactual baseline."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Deadlines and cleanup",
      "assessment": "ContinuousClock supplies a monotonic five-second polling budget; synchronous layout/drawHierarchy work is not preempted at exactly five seconds. Awaited20ms sleep yields MainActor and propagates task cancellation. Existing defer detaches/hides the window, clears/resumes pending continuations through close, and restores the previous key window. Close marks the renderer closed and clears continuations before resuming, retaining its existing duplicate-resume protection."
    }
  ],
